1
00:00:00,290 --> 00:00:02,810
If your knee replacement
still hurts

2
00:00:02,810 --> 00:00:05,470
and the X-ray keeps coming
back fine,

3
00:00:05,470 --> 00:00:07,050
don't accept that.

4
00:00:07,050 --> 00:00:09,330
I've been a pipefitter
for thirty years.

5
00:00:09,330 --> 00:00:10,410
Kneeling in trenches

6
00:00:10,410 --> 00:00:11,730
and mechanical rooms,

7
00:00:11,730 --> 00:00:13,400
day in and day out.

8
00:00:13,400 --> 00:00:14,350
I had my right knee

9
00:00:14,350 --> 00:00:16,150
replaced two years ago.

10
00:00:16,150 --> 00:00:18,290
It has hurt every day
since.

11
00:00:18,290 --> 00:00:19,690
Not surgery pain.

12
00:00:19,690 --> 00:00:20,820
I know what that felt
like,

13
00:00:20,820 --> 00:00:21,920
and it went away.

14
00:00:21,920 --> 00:00:23,130
This is different.

15
00:00:23,130 --> 00:00:23,810
Tight.

16
00:00:23,810 --> 00:00:24,360
Full.

17
00:00:24,360 --> 00:00:25,340
Like a band around

18
00:00:25,340 --> 00:00:27,130
the joint that never
loosens.

19
00:00:27,130 --> 00:00:28,040
And for two years

20
00:00:28,040 --> 00:00:29,580
I've been told the same
thing.

21
00:00:29,580 --> 00:00:30,590
Give it time.

22
00:00:30,590 --> 00:00:32,540
At six weeks it was
swelling,

23
00:00:32,540 --> 00:00:34,140
and swelling is normal.

24
00:00:34,140 --> 00:00:34,930
At three months,

25
00:00:34,930 --> 00:00:36,170
give it six.

26
00:00:36,170 --> 00:00:37,170
At six months,

27
00:00:37,170 --> 00:00:38,930
some knees take a full
year.

28
00:00:38,930 --> 00:00:39,540
At a year,

29
00:00:39,540 --> 00:00:41,450
eighteen months isn't
unusual.

30
00:00:41,450 --> 00:00:42,820
And I didn't just wait.

31
00:00:42,820 --> 00:00:44,190
We went down the list.

32
00:00:44,190 --> 00:00:45,810
More physical therapy.

33
00:00:45,810 --> 00:00:47,060
Every session,

34
00:00:47,060 --> 00:00:48,900
every exercise at home.

35
00:00:48,900 --> 00:00:50,090
I got stronger.

36
00:00:50,090 --> 00:00:51,370
The tightness never moved.

37
00:00:51,370 --> 00:00:53,030
The pain pills helped,

38
00:00:53,030 --> 00:00:54,730
and that was the problem.

39
00:00:54,730 --> 00:00:56,570
I'm already on enough
every morning,

40
00:00:56,570 --> 00:00:57,610
and nobody could tell me

41
00:00:57,610 --> 00:00:59,060
when I'd get to stop.

42
00:00:59,060 --> 00:01:00,920
Then a nerve block.

43
00:01:00,920 --> 00:01:02,980
Then talk of burning the
nerve.

44
00:01:02,980 --> 00:01:04,420
And after that, a second

45
00:01:04,420 --> 00:01:05,780
operation to go back

46
00:01:05,780 --> 00:01:07,260
in and do it over.

47
00:01:07,260 --> 00:01:08,440
I said no.

48
00:01:08,440 --> 00:01:10,160
Every morning I climbed
out of the truck

49
00:01:10,160 --> 00:01:10,980
at the job

50
00:01:10,980 --> 00:01:11,980
and my knee felt like

51
00:01:11,980 --> 00:01:13,780
a band was wrapped around
it,

52
00:01:13,780 --> 00:01:16,410
tightening every inch I
tried to straighten.

53
00:01:16,410 --> 00:01:17,840
Every morning I took
something

54
00:01:17,840 --> 00:01:18,360
for it and

55
00:01:18,360 --> 00:01:19,520
went to work.

56
00:01:19,520 --> 00:01:21,060
Couldn't do the stairs,

57
00:01:21,060 --> 00:01:22,570
couldn't stand at the
counter

58
00:01:22,570 --> 00:01:24,130
long enough to finish
dinner,

59
00:01:24,130 --> 00:01:25,760
couldn't sit through my
granddaughter's

60
00:01:25,760 --> 00:01:28,230
game without shifting
every two minutes.

61
00:01:28,230 --> 00:01:30,270
Couldn't kneel down
under a pipe rack

62
00:01:30,270 --> 00:01:31,400
without grabbing
something

63
00:01:31,400 --> 00:01:32,700
to get back up.

64
00:01:32,700 --> 00:01:33,690
The guys on my crew

65
00:01:33,690 --> 00:01:35,950
started taking the
low work for me.

66
00:01:35,950 --> 00:01:37,170
It woke me at night,

67
00:01:37,170 --> 00:01:39,390
and it turned ordinary
things,

68
00:01:39,390 --> 00:01:40,780
like getting in the car

69
00:01:40,780 --> 00:01:42,080
or up off the couch,

70
00:01:42,080 --> 00:01:43,320
into a decision.

71
00:01:43,320 --> 00:01:44,470
After a long and serious

72
00:01:44,470 --> 00:01:45,620
talk with my wife,

73
00:01:45,620 --> 00:01:47,620
I went back in one more
time.

74
00:01:47,620 --> 00:01:48,650
That was the fourth set

75
00:01:48,650 --> 00:01:50,360
of X-rays on this knee.

76
00:01:50,360 --> 00:01:51,950
And like the three before
it,

77
00:01:51,950 --> 00:01:54,050
the answer was everything
looks great.

78
00:01:54,050 --> 00:01:56,220
No loosening, no
infection,

79
00:01:56,220 --> 00:01:57,440
nothing wrong.

80
00:01:57,440 --> 00:01:58,600
Only this time there

81
00:01:58,600 --> 00:02:00,040
was no new number.

82
00:02:00,040 --> 00:02:01,200
Nobody said

83
00:02:01,200 --> 00:02:03,010
give it another six
months.

84
00:02:03,010 --> 00:02:05,150
There was nothing left to
give it.

85
00:02:05,150 --> 00:02:06,070
I sat in the parking

86
00:02:06,070 --> 00:02:07,100
lot for a while.

87
00:02:07,100 --> 00:02:08,480
Okay, I thought.

88
00:02:08,480 --> 00:02:09,890
Then explain this.

89
00:02:09,890 --> 00:02:12,010
Anyway, a couple of months
back,

90
00:02:12,010 --> 00:02:13,480
I hit my breaking point.

91
00:02:13,480 --> 00:02:15,740
It was around 2:30 in the
morning.

92
00:02:15,740 --> 00:02:17,750
I had a shift
starting at six.

93
00:02:17,750 --> 00:02:19,450
Everyone in the house was
asleep

94
00:02:19,450 --> 00:02:21,520
and I was downstairs in
the recliner

95
00:02:21,520 --> 00:02:22,660
with my leg up,

96
00:02:22,660 --> 00:02:24,430
trying to find any angle
where

97
00:02:24,430 --> 00:02:25,510
it didn't feel like
something

98
00:02:25,510 --> 00:02:27,000
was wrapped around my knee

99
00:02:27,000 --> 00:02:28,300
and tightening.

100
00:02:28,300 --> 00:02:30,830
My wife didn't know I'd
come downstairs.

101
00:02:30,830 --> 00:02:32,570
By then I'd stopped
telling her.

102
00:02:32,570 --> 00:02:33,840
And I just thought,

103
00:02:33,840 --> 00:02:35,540
is this really my life
now?

104
00:02:35,540 --> 00:02:36,990
I can't live like this.

105
00:02:36,990 --> 00:02:38,830
So I made myself a
promise.

106
00:02:38,830 --> 00:02:39,700
I wouldn't go a day

107
00:02:39,700 --> 00:02:41,390
without looking for an
answer.

108
00:02:41,390 --> 00:02:42,850
And when I found one,

109
00:02:42,850 --> 00:02:43,970
I'd share it with everyone

110
00:02:43,970 --> 00:02:45,760
going through the same
thing.

111
00:02:45,760 --> 00:02:46,940
So I got my laptop

112
00:02:46,940 --> 00:02:48,710
out and went looking.

113
00:02:48,710 --> 00:02:49,980
Not for a product.

114
00:02:49,980 --> 00:02:51,500
For an explanation.

115
00:02:51,500 --> 00:02:53,150
Mayo Clinic forums,

116
00:02:53,150 --> 00:02:55,480
the knee replacement group
on Facebook,

117
00:02:55,480 --> 00:02:58,370
doctor videos, medical
animations.

118
00:02:58,370 --> 00:02:59,320
And that's when I found

119
00:02:59,320 --> 00:03:00,940
a video from a physical
therapist

120
00:03:00,940 --> 00:03:01,550
named Dr.

121
00:03:01,550 --> 00:03:03,880
Steven Salinger, whose own
wife

122
00:03:03,880 --> 00:03:05,820
had been through exactly
this.

123
00:03:05,820 --> 00:03:07,540
But before I say anything
else,

124
00:03:07,540 --> 00:03:09,320
I want to be straight with
you.

125
00:03:09,320 --> 00:03:11,430
You've already had
something work fast.

126
00:03:11,430 --> 00:03:12,190
The ice.

127
00:03:12,190 --> 00:03:13,910
The first week of a new
pill.

128
00:03:13,910 --> 00:03:15,530
The good day after a
session.

129
00:03:15,530 --> 00:03:16,700
Then it wore off.

130
00:03:16,700 --> 00:03:19,060
That's the part nobody
warns you about.

131
00:03:19,060 --> 00:03:20,880
Fast relief isn't relief.

132
00:03:20,880 --> 00:03:22,300
It's a preview.

133
00:03:22,300 --> 00:03:23,270
So I'm not going to tell

134
00:03:23,270 --> 00:03:24,530
you this works fast.

135
00:03:24,530 --> 00:03:25,760
It doesn't.

136
00:03:25,760 --> 00:03:27,840
But if you're willing to
be patient,

137
00:03:27,840 --> 00:03:28,640
and to look at what's

138
00:03:28,640 --> 00:03:30,310
going on around your new
knee

139
00:03:30,310 --> 00:03:31,910
instead of inside it,
there

140
00:03:31,910 --> 00:03:34,380
is a real reason it still
hurts.

141
00:03:34,380 --> 00:03:36,690
And something you can do
about it.

142
00:03:36,690 --> 00:03:38,160
Let me explain what he
said,

143
00:03:38,160 --> 00:03:40,280
because this is what
changed

144
00:03:40,280 --> 00:03:41,290
everything for me.

145
00:03:41,290 --> 00:03:43,190
He started with the
basics.

146
00:03:43,190 --> 00:03:44,670
A knee replacement takes
out

147
00:03:44,670 --> 00:03:46,540
the worn joint surfaces
and puts

148
00:03:46,540 --> 00:03:48,230
in metal and plastic.

149
00:03:48,230 --> 00:03:49,960
That's what stops the
arthritis pain

150
00:03:49,960 --> 00:03:51,920
you had before the
operation.

151
00:03:51,920 --> 00:03:53,490
That part I already knew.

152
00:03:53,490 --> 00:03:54,730
But then he explained
something

153
00:03:54,730 --> 00:03:56,120
nobody had ever told me.

154
00:03:56,120 --> 00:03:56,900
He said,

155
00:03:56,900 --> 00:03:58,090
think about a swollen foot

156
00:03:58,090 --> 00:03:59,250
inside a shoe.

157
00:03:59,250 --> 00:04:00,810
The shoe didn't shrink.

158
00:04:00,810 --> 00:04:02,260
Your foot is taking up
more room,

159
00:04:02,260 --> 00:04:03,710
so everything feels
cramped

160
00:04:03,710 --> 00:04:05,380
and tight and squeezed.

161
00:04:05,380 --> 00:04:06,260
Your new knee sits

162
00:04:06,260 --> 00:04:07,630
in a limited space with
living

163
00:04:07,630 --> 00:04:09,610
tissue packed all around
it.

164
00:04:09,610 --> 00:04:11,340
To put that knee in, the
surgeon

165
00:04:11,340 --> 00:04:13,120
had to work through that
tissue.

166
00:04:13,120 --> 00:04:15,740
Afterwards it gets
inflamed and swollen.

167
00:04:15,740 --> 00:04:17,570
At first that's normal.

168
00:04:17,570 --> 00:04:19,490
But in some people that
swelling can

169
00:04:19,490 --> 00:04:22,260
stay switched on far
longer than expected.

170
00:04:22,260 --> 00:04:24,000
And swollen tissue takes
up more

171
00:04:24,000 --> 00:04:26,090
room than calm tissue
does.

172
00:04:26,090 --> 00:04:27,560
So when you bend,

173
00:04:27,560 --> 00:04:29,500
that tissue gets
compressed.

174
00:04:29,500 --> 00:04:30,680
When you straighten,

175
00:04:30,680 --> 00:04:32,120
it gets pulled tight.

176
00:04:32,120 --> 00:04:33,000
That's the band.

177
00:04:33,000 --> 00:04:35,350
That's the ache that never
quite leaves.

178
00:04:35,350 --> 00:04:36,370
And you start being

179
00:04:36,370 --> 00:04:37,530
the one who says,

180
00:04:37,530 --> 00:04:38,720
you go ahead.

181
00:04:38,720 --> 00:04:39,960
I'll stay here.

182
00:04:39,960 --> 00:04:42,080
And that's exactly why so
much

183
00:04:42,080 --> 00:04:44,250
of what I'd tried hadn't
worked.

184
00:04:44,250 --> 00:04:46,470
Physical therapy
strengthens the muscles

185
00:04:46,470 --> 00:04:47,560
around the knee.

186
00:04:47,560 --> 00:04:48,560
Worth doing,

187
00:04:48,560 --> 00:04:49,660
and I'd done it.

188
00:04:49,660 --> 00:04:51,170
It does nothing about
tissue

189
00:04:51,170 --> 00:04:52,390
taking up room.

190
00:04:52,390 --> 00:04:53,820
A nerve block quiets

191
00:04:53,820 --> 00:04:55,920
the nerve carrying the
signal.

192
00:04:55,920 --> 00:04:58,300
It doesn't touch what's
generating it.

193
00:04:58,300 --> 00:04:59,990
But when that irritated
tissue

194
00:04:59,990 --> 00:05:01,440
finally calms down,

195
00:05:01,440 --> 00:05:02,870
it holds less fluid,

196
00:05:02,870 --> 00:05:04,810
and it takes up less room.

197
00:05:04,810 --> 00:05:06,650
Less room taken up means

198
00:05:06,650 --> 00:05:09,020
less pressure squeezing
the joint.

199
00:05:09,020 --> 00:05:11,200
That's what takes the
pressure off.

200
00:05:11,200 --> 00:05:12,740
After two years of this,

201
00:05:12,740 --> 00:05:14,720
it finally made sense.

202
00:05:14,720 --> 00:05:16,760
The problem was never the
new knee.

203
00:05:16,760 --> 00:05:18,740
It was the tissue crowded
around it.

204
00:05:18,740 --> 00:05:20,550
He calls it the squeeze.

205
00:05:20,550 --> 00:05:23,220
Once you've felt it,
that's the word.

206
00:05:23,220 --> 00:05:24,850
I'd bought knee pads,

207
00:05:24,850 --> 00:05:26,260
knee sleeves,

208
00:05:26,260 --> 00:05:28,630
compression braces,
creams,

209
00:05:28,630 --> 00:05:30,240
half of Amazon really,

210
00:05:30,240 --> 00:05:31,300
and all any of it gave me

211
00:05:31,300 --> 00:05:32,460
was an hour.

212
00:05:32,460 --> 00:05:33,410
I even looked at going

213
00:05:33,410 --> 00:05:35,460
to a clinic for the light
therapy.

214
00:05:35,460 --> 00:05:37,150
But at $200 a session

215
00:05:37,150 --> 00:05:38,940
with nothing covered by
insurance,

216
00:05:38,940 --> 00:05:40,980
that was a quick no.

217
00:05:40,980 --> 00:05:41,920
Then one night I went

218
00:05:41,920 --> 00:05:43,200
back to that knee
replacement

219
00:05:43,200 --> 00:05:44,750
group and actually read
it.

220
00:05:44,750 --> 00:05:46,090
Thousands of people,

221
00:05:46,090 --> 00:05:47,860
years out from surgery,

222
00:05:47,860 --> 00:05:50,100
comparing notes on
stiffness and tightness

223
00:05:50,100 --> 00:05:51,600
nobody could explain.

224
00:05:51,600 --> 00:05:53,330
And no matter how far I
scrolled,

225
00:05:53,330 --> 00:05:55,210
the same thing kept coming
up.

226
00:05:55,210 --> 00:05:56,830
This one device,

227
00:05:56,830 --> 00:05:58,830
and people saying it was
the first

228
00:05:58,830 --> 00:06:00,180
thing that made a
difference.

229
00:06:00,180 --> 00:06:02,360
And before anyone jumps in
thinking,

230
00:06:02,360 --> 00:06:03,430
alright, here it comes,

231
00:06:03,430 --> 00:06:04,490
he's selling me something,

232
00:06:04,490 --> 00:06:06,360
let me shut that down
right now.

233
00:06:06,360 --> 00:06:08,200
I'm only here because I
made myself

234
00:06:08,200 --> 00:06:10,370
a promise at 2:30 in the
morning

235
00:06:10,370 --> 00:06:11,320
that if I ever found

236
00:06:11,320 --> 00:06:12,540
something that helped,

237
00:06:12,540 --> 00:06:13,630
I'd say so.

238
00:06:13,630 --> 00:06:14,950
It's called the KenRelief
Red

239
00:06:14,950 --> 00:06:16,600
Light Therapy Wrap.

240
00:06:16,600 --> 00:06:18,820
At first glance I didn't
buy it.

241
00:06:18,820 --> 00:06:19,790
It looked like the cheap

242
00:06:19,790 --> 00:06:21,190
knee sleeves off Amazon

243
00:06:21,190 --> 00:06:22,820
that did nothing for me.

244
00:06:22,820 --> 00:06:24,480
But I went to their
website anyway,

245
00:06:24,480 --> 00:06:25,420
just to see what all

246
00:06:25,420 --> 00:06:26,850
the fuss was about.

247
00:06:26,850 --> 00:06:28,600
It's the same red light
therapy

248
00:06:28,600 --> 00:06:31,380
clinics charge $200 a
session

249
00:06:31,380 --> 00:06:33,470
for, off machines that
cost

250
00:06:33,470 --> 00:06:35,130
fifty thousand dollars,

251
00:06:35,130 --> 00:06:36,280
in a wrap you plug

252
00:06:36,280 --> 00:06:37,890
into the wall at home.

253
00:06:37,890 --> 00:06:39,830
Two hundred and forty
lights.

254
00:06:39,830 --> 00:06:41,830
Red at 660 nanometers

255
00:06:41,830 --> 00:06:44,350
and near-infrared at 850,

256
00:06:44,350 --> 00:06:46,640
run together for the
strongest effect.

257
00:06:46,640 --> 00:06:48,060
Four strength levels.

258
00:06:48,060 --> 00:06:50,000
A five to thirty minute
timer.

259
00:06:50,000 --> 00:06:51,720
Then I saw the guarantee.

260
00:06:51,720 --> 00:06:53,100
Ninety days.

261
00:06:53,100 --> 00:06:55,420
Results or your money
back,

262
00:06:55,420 --> 00:06:57,630
no questions, no store
credit,

263
00:06:57,630 --> 00:06:59,370
and you don't even send it
back.

264
00:06:59,370 --> 00:07:01,390
No physical therapist ever
gave me ninety

265
00:07:01,390 --> 00:07:03,180
days to change my mind.

266
00:07:03,180 --> 00:07:04,900
There wasn't much to lose,

267
00:07:04,900 --> 00:07:05,990
so I ordered it.

268
00:07:05,990 --> 00:07:07,530
Two of them, actually.

269
00:07:07,530 --> 00:07:09,850
Only the right knee was
replaced,

270
00:07:09,850 --> 00:07:12,030
but you favor the leg that
hurts,

271
00:07:12,030 --> 00:07:14,460
and I'd done it for two
years.

272
00:07:14,460 --> 00:07:16,620
The left one was carrying
the difference.

273
00:07:16,620 --> 00:07:17,630
When it came,

274
00:07:17,630 --> 00:07:20,010
I strapped it on expecting
nothing,

275
00:07:20,010 --> 00:07:21,330
because I'd been let down
too

276
00:07:21,330 --> 00:07:23,250
many times to get excited.

277
00:07:23,250 --> 00:07:25,060
What I felt was warmth.

278
00:07:25,060 --> 00:07:27,350
Not a heating pad kind of
hot.

279
00:07:27,350 --> 00:07:29,240
More like it was coming
from inside

280
00:07:29,240 --> 00:07:31,440
the knee and spreading
around it.

281
00:07:31,440 --> 00:07:32,610
And that was it.

282
00:07:32,610 --> 00:07:34,380
That was the whole
experience.

283
00:07:34,380 --> 00:07:35,720
When I took it off,

284
00:07:35,720 --> 00:07:36,760
I'll be honest,

285
00:07:36,760 --> 00:07:38,830
nothing dramatic had
happened.

286
00:07:38,830 --> 00:07:40,890
And after what that video
said,

287
00:07:40,890 --> 00:07:43,300
that's exactly what I
expected.

288
00:07:43,300 --> 00:07:44,100
What was different

289
00:07:44,100 --> 00:07:45,260
was that for the first

290
00:07:45,260 --> 00:07:46,880
time in two years

291
00:07:46,880 --> 00:07:48,830
I'd done something for my
knee

292
00:07:48,830 --> 00:07:50,450
instead of to it.

293
00:07:50,450 --> 00:07:51,280
Twenty minutes,

294
00:07:51,280 --> 00:07:53,580
in my own chair,
after work.

295
00:07:53,580 --> 00:07:55,580
No drive, no copay.

296
00:07:55,580 --> 00:07:57,130
They say twenty minutes.

297
00:07:57,130 --> 00:07:58,240
I did thirty,

298
00:07:58,240 --> 00:07:59,360
twice a day,

299
00:07:59,360 --> 00:08:01,500
lowest setting that first
week.

300
00:08:01,500 --> 00:08:03,120
I put it on the calendar.

301
00:08:03,120 --> 00:08:03,950
The first week,

302
00:08:03,950 --> 00:08:04,840
I couldn't have told

303
00:08:04,840 --> 00:08:06,620
you if anything was
happening.

304
00:08:06,620 --> 00:08:07,560
I tried not to get

305
00:08:07,560 --> 00:08:08,630
my hopes up.

306
00:08:08,630 --> 00:08:10,030
I'd had things help for a
week

307
00:08:10,030 --> 00:08:11,190
and then stop.

308
00:08:11,190 --> 00:08:12,730
But somewhere in the
second week

309
00:08:12,730 --> 00:08:14,000
I noticed I'd come down

310
00:08:14,000 --> 00:08:15,990
the stairs without holding
the rail.

311
00:08:15,990 --> 00:08:17,470
I hadn't decided to.

312
00:08:17,470 --> 00:08:18,540
I just did it,

313
00:08:18,540 --> 00:08:19,960
then stopped halfway down

314
00:08:19,960 --> 00:08:21,500
because I realized.

315
00:08:21,500 --> 00:08:23,100
By the end of the fourth
week

316
00:08:23,100 --> 00:08:24,370
I'd slept through the
night

317
00:08:24,370 --> 00:08:26,030
four times running.

318
00:08:26,030 --> 00:08:27,170
I stood at the counter

319
00:08:27,170 --> 00:08:28,620
and finished making dinner

320
00:08:28,620 --> 00:08:30,540
without looking for the
stool.

321
00:08:30,540 --> 00:08:32,090
None of that is dramatic.

322
00:08:32,090 --> 00:08:33,010
All of it was gone

323
00:08:33,010 --> 00:08:34,260
for two years.

324
00:08:34,260 --> 00:08:35,900
A few weeks later my wife
asked

325
00:08:35,900 --> 00:08:36,840
if I wanted to walk

326
00:08:36,840 --> 00:08:38,670
the long way around the
block.

327
00:08:38,670 --> 00:08:39,540
And for the first time

328
00:08:39,540 --> 00:08:40,280
in two years,

329
00:08:40,280 --> 00:08:41,580
I said yes.

330
00:08:41,580 --> 00:08:43,150
I wanted to understand
why,

331
00:08:43,150 --> 00:08:44,790
so I read the whole thing.

332
00:08:44,790 --> 00:08:46,580
It comes down to four
steps.

333
00:08:46,580 --> 00:08:47,500
One.

334
00:08:47,500 --> 00:08:49,280
The tissue around a new
knee can

335
00:08:49,280 --> 00:08:52,960
stay inflamed long after
surgery is over.

336
00:08:52,960 --> 00:08:53,870
Two.

337
00:08:53,870 --> 00:08:56,480
Inflamed tissue holds
extra fluid,

338
00:08:56,480 --> 00:08:57,400
so it takes up more

339
00:08:57,400 --> 00:08:58,840
room than it should.

340
00:08:58,840 --> 00:08:59,320
Three.

341
00:08:59,320 --> 00:09:01,460
There's only so much room
in there.

342
00:09:01,460 --> 00:09:03,350
Bending compresses it.

343
00:09:03,350 --> 00:09:04,960
Straightening pulls it
tight.

344
00:09:04,960 --> 00:09:06,290
That's the squeeze.

345
00:09:06,290 --> 00:09:07,340
Four.

346
00:09:07,340 --> 00:09:09,090
Red and near-infrared
light have been

347
00:09:09,090 --> 00:09:11,380
studied for calming that
inflammation,

348
00:09:11,380 --> 00:09:12,930
so the swelling and the
pressure

349
00:09:12,930 --> 00:09:14,320
can come down with it.

350
00:09:14,320 --> 00:09:16,120
In a randomized trial,

351
00:09:16,120 --> 00:09:17,940
patients given light
therapy after

352
00:09:17,940 --> 00:09:19,210
a knee replacement

353
00:09:19,210 --> 00:09:20,470
had less pain,

354
00:09:20,470 --> 00:09:21,470
less swelling

355
00:09:21,470 --> 00:09:22,860
and better early movement
than

356
00:09:22,860 --> 00:09:24,000
those who weren't.

357
00:09:24,000 --> 00:09:26,660
A 2025 review said the
same,

358
00:09:26,660 --> 00:09:28,410
and was clear the evidence

359
00:09:28,410 --> 00:09:29,790
is still limited.

360
00:09:29,790 --> 00:09:31,320
I probably sound like a
broken

361
00:09:31,320 --> 00:09:33,530
record to the guys
on my crew.

362
00:09:33,530 --> 00:09:35,540
But after two years of
doing everything

363
00:09:35,540 --> 00:09:37,610
I was told and getting
nowhere,

364
00:09:37,610 --> 00:09:39,060
you have no idea what it's

365
00:09:39,060 --> 00:09:40,800
like to sleep through the
night,

366
00:09:40,800 --> 00:09:42,320
say yes to the walk,

367
00:09:42,320 --> 00:09:43,890
and get my life back.

368
00:09:43,890 --> 00:09:45,470
So take it from me.

369
00:09:45,470 --> 00:09:47,470
Don't spend another year
waiting

370
00:09:47,470 --> 00:09:48,620
for it to settle.

371
00:09:48,620 --> 00:09:50,890
Don't spend two hundred a
session.

372
00:09:50,890 --> 00:09:52,190
More than ten thousand
people

373
00:09:52,190 --> 00:09:53,160
with pain after a knee

374
00:09:53,160 --> 00:09:55,030
replacement have already
tried this.

375
00:09:55,030 --> 00:09:57,090
Some had it worse than I
did.

376
00:09:57,090 --> 00:09:58,280
You can get the KenRelief

377
00:09:58,280 --> 00:09:59,950
wrap from their website,

378
00:09:59,950 --> 00:10:01,470
with a discount link

379
00:10:01,470 --> 00:10:03,580
and ninety days to try it.

380
00:10:03,580 --> 00:10:05,550
If it doesn't do anything
for you,

381
00:10:05,550 --> 00:10:06,950
you get your money back

382
00:10:06,950 --> 00:10:08,410
and you keep the wrap.

383
00:10:08,410 --> 00:10:09,880
They only release so many

384
00:10:09,880 --> 00:10:11,210
